# Privacy Rules

## Local-Only Processing

- All email extraction happens in the content script on the user's device
- No `fetch`, XHR, WebSocket, or external API calls
- No third-party libraries or CDN scripts

## No Tracking

- No analytics SDKs (Google Analytics, Mixpanel, etc.)
- No error reporting services (Sentry, etc.)
- No fingerprinting or device identification

## Data Collection

- Collection starts only on explicit user action (Collect button)
- Collect only publicly visible data from LinkedIn search pages
- Store data in `chrome.storage.local` only

## User Control

- Users can view, copy, and delete collected data
- "Clear All Data" must remove all storage keys
- Document any new data collection in `docs/STORAGE.md` and `PRIVACY.md`

## Chrome Web Store

- Maintain accurate permission justifications
- Keep `PRIVACY.md` in sync with actual data handling
- Single purpose: email collection from LinkedIn search results
